eval("__webpack_require__.r(__webpack_exports__);\n/* harmony export */ __webpack_require__.d(__webpack_exports__, {\n/* harmony export */   DEMO_CASES: () => (/* binding */ DEMO_CASES)\n/* harmony export */ });\nconst DEMO_CASES = [\n    {\n        id: \"space-mission-launch\",\n        title: \"Orbital Lunar Mission Launch\",\n        topic: \"Space Exploration & National Policy\",\n        tagline: \"Three contrasting editorial framings of a landmark national space mission.\",\n        date: \"March 14, 2026\",\n        articles: [\n            {\n                id: \"space-art-1\",\n                title: \"Historic Lunar Ascent: Nation Reaches New Milestone in Cosmic Exploration\",\n                publisher: \"The National Chronicle\",\n                author: \"Aarav Sharma\",\n                date: \"March 14, 2026\",\n                text: `The nation celebrated a monumental triumph yesterday as the ambitious Chandrayaan-IV lunar orbiter roared into the stratosphere from the coastal spaceport. In an unprecedented display of scientific ingenuity, our domestic aerospace engineers achieved flawless separation within minutes of ignition. \n\nGovernment ministers declared that the triumph undoubtedly cements the country's sovereign leadership in the 21st-century cosmic arena. Tens of thousands of jubilant citizens gathered outside the space center, waving national flags and cheering as the rocket pierced the clouds. \n\nOfficials close to the mission confirmed that lunar orbital insertion is guaranteed to proceed without complication. This glorious leap forward sends an unmistakable message across the globe that our technological ascent is unstoppable.`\n            },\n            {\n                id: \"space-art-2\",\n                title: \"Space Agency Launches Costly Lunar Orbiter Amid Growing Domestic Budget Scrutiny\",\n                publisher: \"The Fiscal Tribune\",\n                author: \"Elena Rostova\",\n                date: \"March 14, 2026\",\n                text: `The national space administration launched its multi-billion-dollar Chandrayaan-IV lunar mission on Thursday, intensifying debate over soaring state expenditures amid pressing healthcare and educational shortages. \n\nWhile agency officials touted the launch as a technological achievement, economic analysts warned that the exorbitant capital drain comes at a precarious moment for the national deficit. Critics argue that diverting immense taxpayer funds toward orbital telemetry when rural infrastructure remains desperately underfunded represents a questionable public priority. \n\nIndependent fiscal audits indicate the program has already exceeded initial projections by 38 percent. Furthermore, anonymous sources within the finance ministry quietly suggested that upcoming exploration phases may trigger severe spending freezes across essential civic welfare portfolios.`\n            },\n            {\n                id: \"space-art-3\",\n                title: \"Lunar Rocket Launch Marks Decisive Chess Move in Expanding Asia Space Rivalry\",\n                publisher: \"Global Horizon Dispatch\",\n                author: \"Marcus Vance\",\n                date: \"March 14, 2026\",\n                text: `Thursday's successful launch of the Chandrayaan-IV spacecraft marks a strategic counter-maneuver in the escalating geopolitical contest for lunar surveillance and extraterrestrial resource rights across the Indo-Pacific. \n\nDefense strategists view the orbital platform as a critical dual-use asset designed to challenge Beijing's aggressive space ambitions. Regional defense analysts noted that orbital tracking telemetry provides vital intelligence superiority beyond purely academic exploration. \n\nWestern diplomatic envoys expressed cautious optimism regarding potential data-sharing agreements, though neighboring military commands will inevitably monitor the mission's dual-band communications payloads with heightened vigilance. The launch underscores how orbital space has evolved into the defining frontier of 21st-century great-power competition.`\n            }\n        ]\n    },\n    {\n        id: \"ai-governance-bill\",\n        title: \"Omnibus Artificial Intelligence Safety Act\",\n        topic: \"Technology Regulation & Economic Strategy\",\n        tagline: \"Comparing how tech media, consumer advocates, and financial journals frame frontier AI oversight.\",\n        date: \"February 28, 2026\",\n        articles: [\n            {\n                id: \"ai-art-1\",\n                title: \"Suffocating Bureaucracy: Sweeping AI Bill Threatens to Crush Domestic Innovation\",\n                publisher: \"Silicon Frontier Daily\",\n                author: \"Caleb Henderson\",\n                date: \"February 28, 2026\",\n                text: `Lawmakers passed the controversial Omnibus Artificial Intelligence Safety Act yesterday, delivering a catastrophic blow to the domestic technology sector. The draconian compliance mandates will inevitably force promising machine learning startups to relocate their research labs overseas to escape crippling regulatory bottlenecks. \n\nVenture capitalists warned that the bill's punitive audit standards will freeze early-stage venture funding and hand strategic advantage directly to foreign competitors. \n\nIndustry leaders rightly pointed out that voluntary safety benchmarks were already functioning seamlessly without heavy-handed government intervention. This reckless legislation demonstrates how detached politicians are willing to sacrifice technological dominance for bureaucratic political theater.`\n            },\n            {\n                id: \"ai-art-2\",\n                title: \"Historic Oversight Law Finally Reins In Unaccountable Tech Conglomerates\",\n                publisher: \"Public Citizen Review\",\n                author: \"Amira Patel\",\n                date: \"February 28, 2026\",\n                text: `In a long-overdue victory for civil liberties, the legislature enacted landmark safeguards yesterday to protect citizens from predatory automated systems and unvetted algorithmic discrimination. \n\nConsumer advocacy coalitions celebrated the new statute as a vital barrier against reckless corporate experimentation on the public. For years, secretive tech giants have deployed dangerous automated models without independent scrutiny, evading responsibility for documented biases and workplace displacement. \n\nThe new law mandates rigorous third-party red-teaming, strict disclosure of training datasets, and enforceable fines for algorithmic negligence. Activists noted that while tech lobbyists spent millions spreading fear of economic collapse, the legislation establishes fundamental standards of corporate accountability that put human safety above profit margins.`\n            },\n            {\n                id: \"ai-art-3\",\n                title: \"New AI Framework Establishes Predictable Guardrails for Enterprise Deployment\",\n                publisher: \"Wall Street Capital Ledger\",\n                author: \"Jonathan Sterling\",\n                date: \"February 28, 2026\",\n                text: `The enactment of the Omnibus Artificial Intelligence Safety Act provides global enterprise investors with long-awaited legal clarity, establishing standardized risk tiers for machine learning implementations across banking, healthcare, and infrastructure. \n\nMajor enterprise software providers indicated that the phased two-year implementation timetable offers sufficient runway to align internal governance with new compliance mandates without derailing scheduled enterprise product releases. \n\nMarket analysts observed that while compliance overhead will increase operational expenses for tier-one foundation model developers by an estimated 4 to 6 percent, the clear liability boundaries will likely unlock institutional venture capital that had previously remained on the sidelines awaiting statutory certainty.`\n            }\n        ]\n    },\n    {\n        id: \"climate-transition-accord\",\n        title: \"Clean Energy Transition Mandate\",\n        topic: \"Climate Policy & Energy Markets\",\n        tagline: \"Examining environmentalist, industrial, and market capital framings of statutory net-zero deadlines.\",\n        date: \"January 19, 2026\",\n        articles: [\n            {\n                id: \"energy-art-1\",\n                title: \"Planetary Emergency Demands Immediate Enforcement of Radical Clean Energy Mandates\",\n                publisher: \"The Eco Guardian\",\n                author: \"Rowan Brooks\",\n                date: \"January 19, 2026\",\n                text: `Faced with an escalating climate catastrophe, progressive environmental ministers ratified the Clean Energy Transition Accord yesterday, setting a non-negotiable deadline to phase out dirty fossil power generation by 2032. \n\nClimate scientists urgently warned that any compromise on timelines would result in irreversible ecological devastation and severe weather chaos across vulnerable communities. \n\nYouth climate leaders mobilized outside parliament, demanding immediate revocation of oil exploration subsidies and holding polluters legally accountable for generational ecocide. This decisive action represents our final opportunity to avert civilizational collapse and build a regenerative clean energy future.`\n            },\n            {\n                id: \"energy-art-2\",\n                title: \"Premature Green Deadlines Threaten Grid Collapse and Devastating Industrial Blackouts\",\n                publisher: \"Heavy Industry & Power Digest\",\n                author: \"Gordon MacIntyre\",\n                date: \"January 19, 2026\",\n                text: `Grid operators and manufacturing leaders issued stern warnings yesterday following the government's sudden approval of aggressive 2032 decarbonization targets, declaring that intermittent renewable supply is utterly incapable of supporting continuous industrial baseload demand. \n\nFactory federations projected that mandatory fossil plant retirements without proven long-duration battery storage will cause catastrophic energy shortages, crippling automotive assembly lines and domestic steel fabrication. \n\nIndustry veterans pointed out that current grid infrastructure lacks the high-voltage transmission lines necessary to distribute offshore wind power to manufacturing hubs, guaranteeing sky-high electricity tariffs for ordinary consumers and precipitating severe factory closures.`\n            },\n            {\n                id: \"energy-art-3\",\n                title: \"Clean Energy Mandate Triggers Historic Trillion-Dollar Infrastructure Capital Wave\",\n                publisher: \"Financial Markets Chronology\",\n                author: \"Siddharth Rao\",\n                date: \"January 19, 2026\",\n                text: `Institutional investment funds and renewable infrastructure consortiums are preparing for an unprecedented deployment of private capital following statutory confirmation of the 2032 clean energy transition framework. \n\nPrivate equity syndicates announced initial commitments exceeding $140 billion into next-generation geothermal drilling, grid-scale lithium storage, and automated transmission grid modernization. \n\nAsset managers noted that while legacy coal and gas extraction assets will experience accelerated write-downs, the regulatory clarity unlocks stable, inflation-indexed yields for pension funds and sovereign wealth allocators seeking long-duration ESG opportunities over the next three decades.`\n            }\n        ]\n    }\n];\n//# sourceURL=[module]\n//# sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;charset=utf-8;base64,\n//# sourceURL=webpack-internal:///(ssr)/./lib/demo-data.ts\n");

